
===== 2026-08-05T07:29:32.812694 :: claude -p --permission-mode acceptEdits "You are executing step 6.3 of the workflow-builder plan (_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/implementation-plan.md). Step 6.3: Request hardening.

Step description:
Enforce body-size limits that chunked transfer encoding cannot bypass; validate submitted
`options_source` values server-side against the allowlisted resolvers; cap branding upload size
and count. All rejections use the standard error envelope.
**Done when:** pytest proves an oversized chunked request, an invalid option value, and an oversized upload are each rejected with the envelope and correct status code.

Done when: pytest proves an oversized chunked request, an invalid option value, and an oversized upload are each rejected with the envelope and correct status code.

Working agreements: implement ONLY this step (do not start other steps); follow existing conventions and _dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/contracts.md; run pytest, 'npm run test' and 'npm run build' (frontend/) and get them green BEFORE committing; finish with exactly one commit whose subject contains 'step 6.3'. Do not push."
Step 6.3 is complete and committed (`87bdbb6`).

**What was found:** the 2 MiB JSON limit and the branding size check both trusted `request.content_length` — a header chunked transfer encoding never sends. A probe against Werkzeug 3.1.8 confirmed a terminated chunked stream delivers the full body with `content_length = None`, bypassing both checks. `options_source` config values (voice, style, providers, export profile, caption preset) were accepted unvalidated on save, and the branding library had no count cap.

**Changes:**
- `studio/workflows/routes.py:71` — `_json_body` now does a bounded `request.stream.read(MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES + 1)` instead of a header check, keeps the JSON-content-type requirement (preserves the CORS-preflight defense), and gained `allow_empty` so the DELETE route (`routes.py:349`) uses the same bounded reader.
- `studio/workflows/routes.py:60` — blueprint `RequestEntityTooLarge` handler returns the `413 REQUEST_TOO_LARGE` envelope; `branding_upload` sets per-request `max_content_length = 6 MiB` before multipart parsing (Werkzeug 3.1 enforces it while reading, chunked included) and rejects at 50 stored logos with `409 LIMIT_EXCEEDED` before parsing anything.
- `studio/workflows/options.py:96` — `allowed_option_values(source)`: process-lifetime-cached legal-value sets per allowlisted resolver, fail-open when a resolver is unavailable.
- `studio/workflows/validation.py:191` — `options` fields without static options now validate submitted values against the resolver's list (non-string values rejected safely), so a bad value fails save/import with `422 WORKFLOW_INVALID` naming `configuration.<field>`.

**Verification:** `tests/test_workflow_request_hardening.py` (12 tests) proves all three "done when" rejections with envelope + status assertions, plus positive controls (a small chunked body is actually processed, valid option values save) and fail-open behavior. Full backend suite: **160 passed, 38 subtests, 10 gated live tests skipped** — no regressions, notably all built-in templates still pass validation under the new option-value checks. `contracts.md` §11 and the plan's review status were updated. No frontend code changed.

